{"author":{"id":"2de4467f26c42fb223f4d3ddd5611e7c0513d3daae4c1dc315de039036bc997d"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1779038030,"nonce":"o67LFGSIiR49CRu4+jFgaxEem6k=","message":"Browser review of the first overhaul exposed a real limitation in the CSS-only design: dense content can place a numbered sidenote over a strict margin note, and mobile inline notes still interrupt the paragraph. I am replacing the CSS-only desktop margin behavior with a measured client layout: strict margin notes keep their authorial anchor, numbered sidenotes are packed around them, and mobile/tablet notes are rendered after the containing paragraph instead of at the inline token. The site remains statically exportable; the JS is progressive enhancement over semantic markup.","files":null}]}